--- !yfi/header
version: 1
namespace: edges::nary
visibility: public
--- !node &Ingress
pub port: 443
--- !node &Filter
pub order: 1
--- !node &Backend
pub port: 8080
# Three endpoints, one edge. A three-way relation is not three binary ones and
# is never decomposed into them. The endpoints are written as **paths**, which
# is what a `connections` item is: a reach, exactly as a clause operand is, so
# a bare name resolves against this file and needs no anchor to cross the
# document boundary an alias may not cross (D2.6).
--- !edge &Route
pub connections: [Ingress, Filter, Backend]
# An edge is a node, so an edge may be an endpoint of another edge. That is how
# a relation over relations is written, and it is intended.
--- !edge &Supersedes
pub connections: [Route, Backend]
# `connections: []` is the degenerate edge: a relation with no endpoints yet.
# It is a shape and not a mistake — an edge with no `connections` **member** is
# the mistake, and that is `E0223`.
--- !edge &Planned
pub connections: []
